WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.350
Hi, I'm Cirrus!

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.943
NVIDIA turned the skills people publish for agents into worlds agents train in.

00:00:06.943 --> 00:00:07.649
Here's how.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:13.323
Collective means the training data itself: tasks compiled from what thousands

00:00:13.323 --> 00:00:14.707
of people wrote down.

00:00:18.758 --> 00:00:22.073
A public skill is a folder of written instructions.

00:00:22.073 --> 00:00:26.493
An investigator agent reads one and plans the checkable workflows it teaches.

00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:31.012
For each workflow, it samples six axes, from difficulty to persona.

00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:35.276
A creator agent builds the world, the tests and the rubric, and

00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:37.198
only then writes the reference solution.

00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:41.534
Then two gates, with no model in them: the reference must earn

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:44.470
full reward, and a do-nothing agent must earn zero.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.102
Otherwise, the task is dropped.

00:00:48.092 --> 00:00:49.260
Here's the paper's drawing.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.597
Three of its six panels are model work.

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:55.003
The one that decides what survives is Verify, and it involves

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:56.089
no model at all.

00:00:57.592 --> 00:01:00.848
Twenty-two and a half percent is software engineering.

00:01:00.848 --> 00:01:04.511
Business, marketing, research, design and more together outweigh it.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:08.648
Then reinforcement learning.

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:12.667
One run rewards only tests; another adds a rubric term.

00:01:13.087 --> 00:01:15.975
The first term is the tests' reward, from zero to one.

00:01:16.911 --> 00:01:20.172
S is a judge's score for the trace, from minus five to

00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:21.259
five, reading the rubric.

00:01:21.679 --> 00:01:24.186
So the judge can move the reward by at most point two.

00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:28.328
Outcome-only wins every benchmark.

00:01:28.328 --> 00:01:32.661
But a judge holding the skill prefers the rubric run's work seventy-three

00:01:32.661 --> 00:01:35.911
percent of the time, against fifty-four and a half.

00:01:37.392 --> 00:01:41.288
Collective preference and benchmark pass rate are two objectives; right now we

00:01:41.288 --> 00:01:43.560
can only optimise one at a time.

00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:50.244
To recap: skills become tasks, two model-free gates, and a rubric that

00:01:50.244 --> 00:01:52.088
trades benchmark points for method.

00:01:52.508 --> 00:01:54.635
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:54.635 --> 00:01:55.242
I'm Cirrus.

00:01:55.242 --> 00:01:55.546
Bye!
